<title>PERU: Peru's Banco del Progreso plans $50 mln debt issue.</title>
<headline>Peru's Banco del Progreso plans $50 mln debt issue.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peruvian bank Banco del Progreso plans to issue $50 million worth of debt paper on the local market, a company official said Monday.</p>
<p>As part of the global bond issue, the bank hopes to issue $15 million this year and up to a further $15 million in 1998, Banco del Progreso's financial manager Alejandro Velazco said in an interview.</p>
<p>Banco del Progreso is the 11th largest creditor of Peru's 23 commercial banks.</p>
<p>((-- Marco Aquino, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
</text>
